---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import ToolPage from "@bt/ui/ToolPage.astro";
import AdSlot from "@bt/ui/AdSlot.astro";
import PhotoTool from "@bt/ui/PhotoTool.tsx";
import { PRESETS_BR } from "@bt/ui/photo-presets";
import t from "../../i18n/en.json";
---
<Layout
  bleed
  lang="en"
  title="3x4 photo online for free: crop and print at home | Baitaan"
  description="Make a Brazilian 3x4 photo on your phone and download a 10x15 or A4 sheet ready to print. Free, no sign-up, and your photo is never uploaded."
>
  <ToolPage
    heading="3x4 photo online"
    lead="Choose a photo from your phone, fit your face in the frame and download a 10x15 sheet with several 3x4 photos to print at a print shop or at home."
    updated="Updated: November 2026"
    sourcesHeading="Sources"
    sources={[{ href: "https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/us-visas/visa-information-resources/photos.html", label: "US Department of State: visa photo requirements" }]}
  >
    <PhotoTool client:visible presets={PRESETS_BR} t={t.photo} sheets={["10x15", "a4"]} filePrefix="photo" />

    <Fragment slot="guide">
      <h2>Where 3x4 photos are used</h2>
      <p>School and university ID cards, badges, registration forms, enrolment, club cards and many company documents in Brazil. Always check what the issuer asks for, because many official documents now take the photo on the spot.</p>

      <h2>How to print</h2>
      <ol class="ms-5 list-decimal space-y-1">
        <li>Choose the 10x15 sheet to print on photo paper at a print shop or photo kiosk.</li>
        <li>To print at home, choose A4.</li>
        <li>When printing, use actual size or 100%, without “fit to page”.</li>
        <li>Cut along the grey lines.</li>
      </ol>

      <AdSlot unit="0000000000" label="Advertisement" />

      <h2>Tips for a good photo</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>White or light background, with no shadows.</li>
        <li>Face the camera, no sunglasses, cap or hat.</li>
        <li>Natural light from the front, near a window.</li>
        <li>Phone at eye level, about a metre away.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Photo sizes and how many fit on a sheet</h2>
      <p>Pixels are for printing at 300 dpi. The last two columns show how many photos the tool fits on each sheet.</p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead><tr class="text-muted"><th class="py-2 text-start font-medium">Size</th><th class="py-2 text-end font-medium">Pixels</th><th class="py-2 text-end font-medium">10 × 15 cm sheet</th><th class="py-2 text-end font-medium">A4 sheet</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-t border-hair"><td class="py-2 ">3 × 4 cm (RG, CNH, work card, badges)</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">354 × 472</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">8</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">36</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-hair"><td class="py-2 ">5 × 7 cm (forms and some foreign passports)</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">591 × 827</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">2</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">12</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-hair"><td class="py-2 ">5 × 5 cm (US visa)</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">600 × 600</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">2</td><td class="py-2 text-end tabular-nums">15</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>The Brazilian passport doesn't use a printed photo: the Federal Police take it at the appointment. For the US visa, the photo is also sent as a square digital file of at least 600 × 600 pixels.</p>
      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <details class="bt-faq"><summary>Can I print at home?</summary><p>Yes, on photo paper with the actual size or 100% option. At a stationery shop, the 10 × 15 cm sheet prints on photo paper cheaply and looks better.</p></details>
      <details class="bt-faq"><summary>What if the photo is rejected?</summary><p>The usual reasons are a shadowed or coloured background, a tilted face, glasses reflecting light and printing with “fit to page”, which changes the size. Retake the photo by a window and print at 100%.</p></details>
      <details class="bt-faq"><summary>Is my photo sent anywhere?</summary><p>No. Cropping and the sheet are done in your browser, and the photo never leaves your device.</p></details>
    </Fragment>
  </ToolPage>
</Layout>
